Sibling issue: https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/issues/85806

**Version Used:** dotnet/roslyn `main`

**Steps to Reproduce:**
```csharp
var source = """
    #nullable enable
    public class C
    {
        public void M(string? s = default) { }
    }
    """;
var tree = CSharpSyntaxTree.ParseText(source);
var compilation = CSharpCompilation.Create("c", new[] { tree }, ...);
var model = compilation.GetSemanticModel(tree);

var parameter = tree.GetRoot().DescendantNodes().OfType<ParameterSyntax>().Single();
var position = parameter.Default!.SpanStart;

// Built via SyntaxFactory, not tree.ReplaceNode(...) - both reproduce identically, confirming
// the fix is general, not tied to how the node was constructed.
var speculativeInitializer = SyntaxFactory.EqualsValueClause(SyntaxFactory.ParseExpression("null"));

model.TryGetSpeculativeSemanticModel(position, speculativeInitializer, out var speculativeModel);
var typeInfo = speculativeModel.GetTypeInfo(speculativeInitializer.Value);
// typeInfo.Nullability.FlowState is None. Expected: MaybeNull (matching what a real
// analysis of `string? s = null` under #nullable enable would report).
```

**Diagnostic Id:** N/A (API behavior, not a diagnostic)

**Expected Behavior:** `Nullability.FlowState = MaybeNull`.

**Actual Behavior:** `Nullability.FlowState` is `None`.

**Root Cause:**

`InitializerSemanticModel.IsNullableAnalysisEnabledCore()`, for `SymbolKind.Parameter`, does:
```csharp
return SourceComplexParameterSymbolBase.GetDefaultValueSyntaxForIsNullableAnalysisEnabled(Root as ParameterSyntax) is { } value &&
    Compilation.IsNullableAnalysisEnabledIn(value);
```
`Root as ParameterSyntax` fails unconditionally: for this speculation, `Root` is always the bare `EqualsValueClauseSyntax` — there is no path that produces a `ParameterSyntax`-shaped `Root`. `GetBoundRoot()` in the same class already tolerates `Root` being either shape; `IsNullableAnalysisEnabledCore()` doesn't.

**Proposed Fix** (for illustration, not a final PR against `main`): https://github.com/martin-strecker-sonarsource/roslyn/pull/4

Reuses `SyntaxTreeSemanticModel.IsNullableAnalysisEnabledAtSpeculativePosition(int, SyntaxNode)` — the same helper `SpeculativeMemberSemanticModel.IsNullableAnalysisEnabledCore()` already uses for `TypeSyntax` speculation — as the fallback when `Root` isn't a `ParameterSyntax`. Validated with zero regressions against `NullableReferenceTypesTests.cs` (4489 passed) and `NullablePublicAPITests`/`SemanticModelGetSemanticInfoTests` (587 passed). The branch is stacked on a reproducer-only PR for review convenience; the actual fix is a small, self-contained diff.

Can you confirm this is indeed a bug, and would a PR implementing a fix along these lines be welcome?



